(78, 'Baku', '77', '77', 'Day Trip', NULL, NULL, NULL, '09:00 – Leaving Baku to Shahdag (1 way x 3 hrs)   12:00 – Shahdag to Candy Cane Mountain - Candy Cane Mountains are a psychedelic, red-pink and white striped area of exposed rock in the Northwest of Azerbaijan. Iron in the ground gives the mountains their deep red color and powdery shale makes up the white parts. Through a geological process, they’ve mixed together underground, layer on top of layer, and when exposed to the elements, they eroded into a beautiful, completely bizarre sight    13:30 – Lunch break  14:30 - Reaching to Shahdag and visit Shahdag Mountains - Shahdag is the highest part of the side ridge in the territory of the Republic of Azerbaijan. It is separated from the Kyzylgaya plateau by the Gusar river valley. composed of sediments of the Jurassic and Cretaceous systems. Its height is up to 4243 meters (Shahdag peak). There are alpine and subalpine meadows, glaciers with an area of more than 1 square km.   Discover the wonders of Shahdag, a land of ancient glaciers, majestic valleys, and stunning mountain lakes! Designed with avid outdoor enthusiasts in mind, Shahdag Mountain Resort offers an array of thrilling activities throughout the year. Picture yourself zooming down the slopes, feeling the crisp mountain air on your face as you carve your way through powdery snow. And for those seeking an adrenaline rush of a different kind, don\'t miss the Shahdag Coaster, an exhilarating roller coaster that takes you on a wild ride through the breathtaking mountain scenery.   17:30 – Leaving Shahdag to Baku   20:30 - Dinner Break (if included)   21:30 – Drop to Hotel  Overnight at Hotel', NULL, NULL, 'Sedan - 4 Seaters (Local Speaking)', 77.00, '2026-02-21 12:16:25'),
