(1, 'Airport', 'Hotel', '1 way Transfer', NULL, NULL, NULL, '- Pick-up from GYD Airport (1 way x 35 mins) \n\n- Drop to Hotel', 12.00, 18.00, 12.00, 24.00, 35.00, 47.00, 59.00, 74.00, 74.00, 20.00, 24.00),
(2, 'Airport', 'Hotel - Airport', '2 ways Transfer', NULL, NULL, NULL, '- Pick-up from GYD Airport (Arrival) - (1 way x 35 mins) \n- Drop-off at the Hotel\n- Pick-up from Hotel (Departure) - (1 way x 35 mins) \n- Drop-off at the GYD Airport', 18.00, 24.00, 18.00, 30.00, 70.00, 94.00, 108.00, 148.00, 148.00, 20.00, 48.00),
(3, 'Baku', 'Shamakhi', 'Day Trip', NULL, NULL, NULL, '09:00 – Leaving Baku to Shamakhi (1 way x 2 hrs)\n\n11:30 – Arrive to Shamakhi\n\n12:00 -  Alpaca Farm is located in the Shamakhi district, close to the Meyseri vineyards, surrounded by picturesque mountains and green pastures. For the construction of the farm, the Shamakhi district was not chosen by chance. Most of this area is a resort area with multiple springs. It is rich in mountain forests and meadows, and is located in a zone of moderate humidity, which makes it ideal for keeping alpacas.In addition, on the territory of the farm there will be souvenir shops with handmade dolls, stationery, bags of fertilizer, branded merch (T-shirts, hoodies, caps).\n\n12:30 – Lunch Break\n\n15:00 -Leave Shamakhi to Baku\n\n18:00 – Dinner Break (if included)\n\n19:30 – Drop to Hotel\n\nOvernight in Shamakhi', 41.00, 47.00, 53.00, 65.00, 165.00, 236.00, 295.00, 354.00, 354.00, 20.00, 47.00),
(4, 'Baku', 'Shamakhi - Baku Panoramic City Tour', 'Private Transfer', NULL, NULL, NULL, '09:00 – Leaving Baku to Shamakhi (1 way x 2 hours)\n\n11:30 – Arrive to Shamakhi\n\n12:00 -  Alpaca Farm is located in the Shamakhi district, close to the Meyseri vineyards, surrounded by picturesque mountains and green pastures. For the construction of the farm, the Shamakhi district was not chosen by chance. Most of this area is a resort area with multiple springs. It is rich in mountain forests and meadows, and is located in a zone of moderate humidity, which makes it ideal for keeping alpacas.In addition, on the territory of the farm there will be souvenir shops with handmade dolls, stationery, bags of fertilizer, branded merch (T-shirts, hoodies, caps).\n\n12:30 – Lunch break\n\n15:00 -Leave Shamakhi to Baku\n\n18:00 – Arrive Baku and start Panaromic city tour\nEvening City Tour starts with panoramic full evening city view of Baku followed by:\n- Highland Park (Which is the highest point in the Azerbaijani capital, opening a panoramic view of the city and its bay. The city\'s residents and visitors often come here to see a bird\'s eye view of Baku, and just have a walk. The Upland Park can be reached by cable railway (funicular) in 7-8 minutes from the boulevard or by climbing up the endless stone stairs.)\n- Flame Towers (The city\'s tallest building. The height of 182 m. Flame Towers - consisting of three high-rise buildings in the complex.)\n\n19:00 - Dinner Break (if included)\n\n20:00 – Drop to Hotel\n\nOvernight at Hotel', 47.00, 53.00, 59.00, 71.00, 195.00, 295.00, 383.00, 427.00, 427.00, 20.00, 47.00),
(5, 'Baku', 'Shamakhi', 'Overnight', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Baku to Shamakhi \n\n09:00 – Leaving Baku to Shamakhi (1 way x 2 hrs)\n\n11:30 – Arrive to Shamakhi\n\n12:00 -  Alpaca Farm is located in the Shamakhi district, close to the Meyseri vineyards, surrounded by picturesque mountains and green pastures. For the construction of the farm, the Shamakhi district was not chosen by chance. Most of this area is a resort area with multiple springs. It is rich in mountain forests and meadows, and is located in a zone of moderate humidity, which makes it ideal for keeping alpacas.In addition, on the territory of the farm there will be souvenir shops with handmade dolls, stationery, bags of fertilizer, branded merch (T-shirts, hoodies, caps).\n\n13:00 – Lunch break\n\n15:00 - Check-in to the Hotel\n\n18:00 - Dinner Break(if included)\n\n19:00 –  Drop to Hotel\n\nOvernight in Shamakhi', 77.00, 83.00, 89.00, 101.00, 225.00, 324.00, 445.00, 560.00, 560.00, 50.00, 65.00),
(6, 'Baku', 'Guba', 'Day Trip', NULL, NULL, NULL, '09:00 – Leaving Baku to Guba(1 way takes 3 hours)\n\n12:00 – Reaching to Guba and visiting the Guba Genocide Memorial Complex.\n The mass grave, discovered accidentally during the excavations for construction purposes in the town of Guba in 2007, was a clear evidence of the genocide of the Muslim population of Guba, committed by Armenian armed forces under Bolshevik name in May 1918. The area is wonderful on the left side of river Qudiyal-chay. Here you can see the part of history of our nation and relax with nature\n\n12:30 – Lunch break\n\n15:00 - Visiting Qecresh Forest \n - Qechresh Forest, also known as Gachresh Forest, is one of the largest forests in Azerbaijan, located near the town of Quba. Renowned for its dense foliage and majestic landscape, it features a rich biodiversity and is a habitat for various plant species and wildlife. The forest\'s high altitude and clean, fresh air make it a perfect spot for those looking for outdoor adventures or simply to relax .\n \n17:00 - Leave Guba to Baku\n\n 20:00 - Dinner Break (if included)\n\n 21:00 – Drop to Hotel\n\nOvernight at Hotel', 71.00, 76.00, 80.00, 85.00, 195.00, 265.00, 324.00, 354.00, 354.00, 20.00, 47.00),
(7, 'Baku', 'Guba', 'Overnight', NULL, NULL, NULL, '09:00 – Leaving Baku to Guba ( 1 way takes 3 hours)\n \n12:00 – Reaching to Guba and visiting the Guba Genocide Memorial Complex.\n- The mass grave, discovered accidentally during the excavations for construction purposes in the town of Guba in 2007, was a clear evidence of the genocide of the Muslim population of Guba, committed by Armenian armed forces under Bolshevik name in May 1918. The area is wonderful on the left side of river Qudiyal-chay. Here you can see the part of history of our nation and relax with nature\n \n12:30 – Lunch Break\n\n15:00 - Check-in to the Hotel 16:00 - Visiting Qecresh Forest \n- Qechresh Forest, also known as Gachresh Forest, is one of the largest forests in Azerbaijan, located near the town of Quba. Renowned for its dense foliage and majestic landscape, it features a rich biodiversity and is a habitat for various plant species and wildlife. The forest\'s high altitude and clean, fresh air make it a perfect spot for those looking for outdoor adventures or simply to relax .\n \n18:00 - Dinner Break (if included)\n \n19:00 – Drop to Hotel\n \nOvernight in Guba', 107.00, 112.00, 116.00, 121.00, 255.00, 353.00, 474.00, 560.00, 560.00, 40.00, 65.00),
(8, 'Baku', 'Shahdagh', 'Day Trip', NULL, NULL, NULL, '09:00 – Leaving Baku to Guba ( 1 way x 3 hrs)\n \n12:00 – Visiting Qecresh Forest (photostop)\n- Qechresh Forest, also known as Gachresh Forest, is one of the largest forests in Azerbaijan, located near the town of Quba. Renowned for its dense foliage and majestic landscape, it features a rich biodiversity and is a habitat for various plant species and wildlife. The forest\'s high altitude and clean, fresh air make it a perfect spot for those looking for outdoor adventures or simply to relax .\n \n12:30 – Lunch Break \n\n13:30 – Reaching to Shahdag and visit Shahdag Mountain Resort\n- Shahdag is the highest part of the side ridge in the territory of the Republic of Azerbaijan. It is separated from the Kyzylgaya plateau by the Gusar river valley. Composed of sediments of the Jurassic and Cretaceous systems. Its height is up to 4243 meters (Shahdag peak). There are alpine and subalpine meadows, glaciers with an area of more than 1 square km. Discover the wonders of Shahdag, a land of ancient glaciers, majestic valleys, and stunning mountain lakes! Designed with avid outdoor enthusiasts in mind, Shahdag Mountain Resort offers an array of thrilling activities throughout the year. Picture yourself zooming down the slopes, feeling the crisp mountain air on your face as you carve your way through powdery snow. And for those seeking an adrenaline rush of a different kind, don\'t miss the Shahdag Coaster, an exhilarating roller coaster that takes you on a wild ride through the breathtaking mountain scenery.\n\n17:00 - Leaving Shahdag to Baku \n\n20:00 - Dinner Break (if included)\n \n21:00 – Drop to Hotel\n\nOvernight at Hotel', 71.00, 76.00, 80.00, 85.00, 195.00, 265.00, 324.00, 354.00, 354.00, 20.00, 47.00),
