(37, 'Gabala', 'Ismayilli', 'Day Trip', NULL, NULL, NULL, '09:00 – Leaving Gabala to Ismayilli (1 way x 1.5 hrs)\n\n 10:45 – Visit Lahij Village (Optional)\n - Lahij is a historic mountain village famous for its cobbled streets, traditional handicrafts (copperware, carpets), and stone architecture. Visitors can see artisans at work, buy souvenirs, and enjoy panoramic mountain views.\n\n 12:15 – Explore Ismayilli City / Nature Spots\n Visit local parks, rivers, or small mountain trails around Ismayilli. Optional short lunch stop in a local restaurant to taste Azerbaijani cuisine.\n\n 14:30 – Lunch Break 15:30 – Visit Basgal Village (Optional)\n Another charming village nearby, known for its history and traditional craft workshops.\n\n 16:00 – Depart from Ismayilli back to Gabala \n\n 17:30 – Arrive back in Gabala\n\n 18:00 - Dinner break (if included) \n\n19:00 - Drop to the Hotel Overnight in Gabala', 30.00, 36.00, 47.00, 59.00, 100.00, 120.00, 120.00, 200.00, 200.00, 20.00, 47.00),
(38, 'Gabala', 'Sheki', 'Day Trip', NULL, NULL, NULL, '08:00 – Leaving Gabala to Sheki (1 way x 1.5 hrs)\n\n 09:30 – Arrive in Sheki\n\n 09:45 – Visit Church of Kish\n - Kish is one of the oldest villages in Azerbaijan, famous for its ancient Church of Saint Elisha, dating from the 10th–12th centuries. Scholars believe the church stands on the original site founded by St. Elisha, making it one of the oldest spiritual centers in the Caucasus.\n\n 10:45 – Explore Sheki Fortress\n - Built to protect the historic city center (now a UNESCO World Heritage Site), the fortress originally had 8-meter-high walls and 2-meter-thick fortifications with defensive towers and arched gateways. Some parts have been restored, allowing visitors to experience its historic significance.\n\n 11:45 – Visit Sheki Karavansaray\n - This Silk Road caravanserai historically provided safe lodging for merchants traveling with camels and goods. Today, it is one of Sheki’s iconic landmarks and a must-see cultural site.\n\n 12:30 – Taste Sheki Halva\n - Enjoy Sheki’s famous traditional halva — one of the region’s most beloved culinary specialties.\n\n 13:00 – Lunch Break \n\n 14:00 – Arrive back in Gabala \n\n 18:00 – Dinner Break (if included) \n\n 19:00 – Drop to the Hotel\n\n Overnight in Gabala', 30.00, 36.00, 47.00, 59.00, 100.00, 120.00, 147.00, 177.00, 177.00, 20.00, 47.00),
(39, 'Baku', 'Besbarmaq Mountains', 'Day Trip', NULL, NULL, NULL, '09:00 – Leaving Baku to Beshbarmag (1 way x 1.5 hrs)\n\n10:30 – Arrive at Beshbarmag Mountain \n\n10:45 – Visit Beshbarmag Mountain\n • Beshbarmag (literally “Five Fingers Mountain”) stands at about 382 m / ≈ 500 m above sea level and is a famous natural and spiritual landmark near the Caspian Sea. \n • The hike/trail from the car park to the rocky peak (or sacred “pir / shrine” zone) is fairly accessible; many visit to enjoy the views of the sea and surrounding plains, or for its local spiritual significance. \n \n12:30 – Leaving Beshbarmag to Baku (1 way x 1,5 hrs)\n \n14:00 – Lunch Break \n \n15:00 – Drop to the Hotel \n  \n Overnight in Baku', 30.00, 36.00, 47.00, 59.00, 165.00, 236.00, 295.00, 354.00, 354.00, 20.00, 47.00),
(40, 'Baku', 'Red Bridge', '1 way Transfer', NULL, NULL, NULL, '08:30 – Leaving Baku to Red Bridge (1 way x 6,5 hrs)\n\n 14:00 – Lunch Break\n\n 14:15 – Visit and explore Red Bridge - The Red Bridge is a historical architectural monument built over the Khrami (or “Khram”) river, known for its red brick construction. The structure dates back to the 12th/17th centuries and has four spans. In the past, the area around the bridge included caravanserai style accommodations for merchants traveling along major trade routes. \n\n 15:00 – Leaving Red Bridge back to Baku \n\n 21:00 – Dinner Break (if included) (1 way x 6,5 hrs)\n\n 22:00 – Drop to the Hotel \n\n Overnight in Baku', 65.00, 71.00, 112.00, 124.00, 324.00, 412.00, 471.00, 530.00, 530.00, 40.00, 47.00),
(41, 'Baku', 'Laqodexi', '1 way Transfer', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Leaving Baku to Laqodexi Border (1 way x 7 hrs)\n\n- Travel distance: 450 km\n\n- The route is mainly highway, with scenic mountain views along parts of the way.\n\n- Arrive at Laqodexi / Azerbaijan–Georgia Border', 89.00, 95.00, 112.00, 124.00, 324.00, 412.00, 471.00, 530.00, 530.00, 40.00, 47.00),
(42, 'Gabala', 'Sheki-Ganja', 'Day Trip', NULL, NULL, NULL, '08:00 – Leaving Gabala to Sheki (1 way x 1.5 hrs)\n\n 09:30 – Arrive at Sheki \n\n - Church of Kish – An ancient church dating back to the 10–12th centuries, one of the oldest spiritual centers in the Caucasus.\n - Sheki Fortress – Historic fortress with partial restoration, originally built to protect the city center.\n - Sheki Karavansaray – A Silk Road inn used by merchants, now a cultural landmark.\n - Sheki Halva Tasting – Traditional sweet specialty, highly recommended for visitors.\n\n 12:30 - Lunch Break \n\n 13:30 – Leaving Sheki to Ganja (1 way x 2.5 hrs)\n\n 16:00 – Arrive at Ganja\n\n - Nizami Ganjavi Mausoleum – Honoring Azerbaijan’s famous poet, featuring a beautifully restored monument and crypt.\n - Javad Khan Tomb – Memorial to Ganja’s last khan, who defended the city; a historical landmark.\n - Javad Khan Street – Central street showcasing Ganja’s architectural heritage and cultural vibe.\n\n 18:00 – Leaving Ganja to Gabala\n\n 20:30 – Dinner Break (if included) \n\n 21:30 – Drop to the hotel\n\nOvernight in Gabala', 71.00, 77.00, 89.00, 101.00, 147.00, 165.00, 177.00, 206.00, 206.00, 20.00, 47.00),
(43, 'Sheki', 'Ganja', 'Day Trip', NULL, NULL, NULL, '09:00 – Leaving Sheki to Ganja (1 way x 2.5 hrs)\n \n11:30 – Arrive in Ganja\n - Nizami Ganjavi Mausoleum\n - Monument honoring Azerbaijan’s famous poet Nizami Ganjavi.\n - Features a restored mausoleum and poet’s crypt; surrounded by a square with sculptures representing Nizami’s Khamsa.\n\n 12:30 – Javad Khan Tomb\n • Memorial to Ganja’s last khan, who defended the city.\n • Historical site reflecting the city’s past struggles and heroism. \n\n 14:00 – Lunch Break\n\n 15:00 – Javad Khan Street\n • One of Ganja’s central streets, showcasing the city’s architectural heritage and cultural atmosphere.\n\n 16:00 – Leaving Ganja to Sheki (1 way x 2.5 hrs)\n\n 18:30 –Dinner Break (if included) \n\n 19:30 - Drop to the Hotel\n \n Overnight in Sheki', 59.00, 65.00, 71.00, 83.00, 118.00, 130.00, 147.00, 177.00, 177.00, 20.00, 47.00),
(44, 'Hotel', 'Gobustan + Old City Tour', 'Private Transfer', NULL, NULL, NULL, '09:00 – Leaving from Baku to Gobustan (1 way x 45 mins)\n\n 10:00 – Arrive at Gobustan National Park\n - Visit Gobustan National Park, a UNESCO World Heritage site known for its ancient petroglyphs, rock formations, and archaeological heritage dating back more than 40,000 years. The open-air museum offers insights into prehistoric human life, hunting traditions, and early settlements. After exploring the site, continue to the nearby Mud Volcanoes—one of the largest mud volcano fields in the world. The unique grey, lunar-like landscape and constantly bubbling mud pools create an unforgettable natural experience and an excellent spot for photos.\n\n 12:00 – Leaving Gobustan to Baku (1 way x 45 mins)\n\n 13:00 – Lunch Break\n\n 14:00 - Old City tour starts from Shamakhi Gates followed by below places (Photo stop).\n - Shamakhi Gates – The historic entrance to the Old City, showcasing iconic stone architecture.\n - Sculptures of Azim Azimzadeh – Artistic monuments honoring Azerbaijan’s famed satirical painter and graphic artist.\n - Caravanserai of Bukhara – A restored medieval inn once used by Silk Road traders for rest and trade.\n - Caravanserai of Multani – A traditional guesthouse built for merchants from Multan, reflecting oriental caravan culture.\n - Maiden’s Tower – Baku’s mysterious UNESCO-listed tower offering panoramic views of the Old City.\n - Bazar Square – A lively historic square once serving as the commercial heart of Icherisheher.\n - Miniature Books’ Museum – A unique museum displaying one of the world’s largest collections of tiny books.\n - Shirvanshahs’ Palace – A majestic 15th-century royal complex showcasing medieval Azerbaijani architecture.\n \n 18:00 – Dinner Break (if includes)\n\n 19:00 – Drop to the Hotel \n\n Overnight in Baku', 41.00, 47.00, 47.00, 59.00, 130.00, 147.00, 177.00, 206.00, 206.00, 20.00, 47.00);
