(45, 'Hotel', 'Gobustan + Nizami Street', 'Private Transfer', NULL, NULL, NULL, '09:00 – Leaving from Baku to Gobustan (1 way x 45 mins)\n\n10:00 – Arrive at Gobustan National Park\n - Visit Gobustan National Park, a UNESCO World Heritage site known for its ancient petroglyphs, rock formations, and archaeological heritage dating back more than 40,000 years. The open-air museum offers insights into prehistoric human life, hunting traditions, and early settlements. After exploring the site, continue to the nearby Mud Volcanoes—one of the largest mud volcano fields in the world. The unique grey, lunar-like landscape and constantly bubbling mud pools create an unforgettable natural experience and an excellent spot for photos.\n\n12:00 – Leaving Gobustan to Baku (1 way x 45 mins)\n \n13:00 – Lunch Break\n \n14:00 – Visiting Nizami Streets\n\n • One of the city’s main pedestrian streets known for shopping, cafés, and historic architecture. Popular walking area with boutiques, souvenir shops, and local restaurants.\n\n18:00 – Dinner Break (if includes)\n\n19:00 – Drop to the Hotel \n\nOvernight in Baku', 41.00, 47.00, 47.00, 59.00, 130.00, 147.00, 177.00, 206.00, 206.00, 20.00, 47.00),
(46, 'Hotel', 'Gobustan + Boulevard Tour', 'Private Transfer', NULL, NULL, NULL, '09:00 – Leaving from Baku to Gobustan (1 way x 45 mins)\n\n10:00 – Arrive at Gobustan National Park\n - Visit Gobustan National Park, a UNESCO World Heritage site known for its ancient petroglyphs, rock formations, and archaeological heritage dating back more than 40,000 years. The open-air museum offers insights into prehistoric human life, hunting traditions, and early settlements. After exploring the site, continue to the nearby Mud Volcanoes—one of the largest mud volcano fields in the world. The unique grey, lunar-like landscape and constantly bubbling mud pools create an unforgettable natural experience and an excellent spot for photos.\n \n12:00 – Leaving Gobustan to Baku (1 way x 45 mins)\n\n13:00 – Lunch Break\n\n14:00 – Baku Boulevard tour starts along the Boulevard (Photostop) by followed places: \n - Mini Venice of Baku – A charming canal area where you can enjoy gondola-style boat rides in the heart of the city.\n - Deniz Mall – A modern seafront shopping and entertainment center with restaurants, cinemas, and family attractions.\n - Ferris Wheel – A scenic observation wheel offering beautiful panoramic views of the Caspian Sea and Baku Boulevard.\n - Carpet Museum – A uniquely designed museum showcasing Azerbaijan’s rich carpet-weaving heritage and centuries-old masterpieces.\n - Crystal Hall – A spectacular indoor arena famous for hosting major concerts and international events.\n\n 18:00 – Dinner Break (if includes)\n\n 19:00 – Drop to the Hotel \n \nOvernight in Baku', 41.00, 47.00, 47.00, 59.00, 130.00, 147.00, 177.00, 206.00, 206.00, 20.00, 47.00),
(47, 'Hotel', 'Gobustan + Panaromic City Tour', 'Private Transfer', NULL, NULL, NULL, '09:00 – Leaving from Baku to Gobustan (1 way x 45 mins)\n\n10:00 – Arrive at Gobustan National Park\n - Visit Gobustan National Park, a UNESCO World Heritage site known for its ancient petroglyphs, rock formations, and archaeological heritage dating back more than 40,000 years. The open-air museum offers insights into prehistoric human life, hunting traditions, and early settlements. After exploring the site, continue to the nearby Mud Volcanoes—one of the largest mud volcano fields in the world. The unique grey, lunar-like landscape and constantly bubbling mud pools create an unforgettable natural experience and an excellent spot for photos.\n\n12:00 – Leaving Gobustan to Baku\n\n13:00 – Lunch Break\n\n14:00 –Evening City Tour starts with panoramic full evening city view of Baku followed by:\n - Highland Park (Which is the highest point in the Azerbaijani capital, opening a panoramic view of the city and its bay. The city\'s residents and visitors often come here to see a bird\'s eye view of Baku, and just have a walk. The Upland Park can be reached by cable railway (funicular) in 7-8 minutes from the boulevard or by climbing up the endless stone stairs.)\n - Flame Towers (The city\'s tallest building. The height of 182 m. Flame Towers - consisting of three high-rise buildings in the complex.)\n \n18:00 – Dinner Break (if includes)\n\n19:00 – Drop to the Hotel \n \nOvernight in Baku', 41.00, 47.00, 47.00, 59.00, 130.00, 147.00, 177.00, 206.00, 206.00, 20.00, 47.00),
(48, 'Hotel', 'Gobustan + Heydar Aliyev Centre', 'Private Transfer', NULL, NULL, NULL, '09:00 – Leaving Baku to Gobustan (1 way x 45 mins)\n\n 10:00 – Arrive at Gobustan National Park\n - Visit Gobustan National Park, a UNESCO World Heritage site known for its ancient petroglyphs, rock formations, and archaeological heritage dating back more than 40,000 years. The open-air museum offers insights into prehistoric human life, hunting traditions, and early settlements. After exploring the site, continue to the nearby Mud Volcanoes—one of the largest mud volcano fields in the world. The unique grey, lunar-like landscape and constantly bubbling mud pools create an unforgettable natural experience and an excellent spot for photos.\n\n12:00 – Leaving Gobustan to Baku\n\n13:00 – Lunch Break\n\n14:00 –Visit to Heydar Aliyev Center & “I LOVE BAKU” sign Photostop\n - If it’s first time of your arrival to Baku, just be aware of that from the bird view you can clearly see the Heydar Aliyev’s \n Signature on the Heydar Aliyev’s Center design. It’s a wave-like\n building rises from a bed of concrete. Its immobile white walls \n look as though they have been frozen mid-ripple. The abstract \n architecture is unlike anything else in the capital city. The \n Heydar Aliyev Center, which was designed by renowned architect Zaha Hadid.\n \n 18:00 – Dinner Break (if includes)\n\n19:00 – Drop to the Hotel \n \nOvernight in Baku', 41.00, 47.00, 47.00, 59.00, 130.00, 147.00, 177.00, 206.00, 206.00, 20.00, 47.00),
(49, 'Hotel', 'Gobustan + Absheron Tour', 'Private Transfer', NULL, NULL, NULL, '10:00 – Leaving Baku to Absheron (1 way x 30 mins)\n\n 10:30 – Visit to Fire Temple (Ateshgah)\n - An ancient Zoroastrian site where flames were historically kept burning as part of religious rituals. The temple provides insight into Azerbaijan’s early religious history and Zoroastrian culture. Visitors can explore the site and learn about the traditions of fire worship.\n\n 11.30 - Burning Mountains (Yanardag)\n- A natural gas hillside that has been burning continuously for decades, creating a unique “burning mountain” phenomenon. It is a famous landmark of Azerbaijan, offering visitors spectacular views and a memorable experience of the country’s natural fiery landscape.\n \n12:00 – Leaving Absheron to Baku\n \n12:30 – Lunch Break\n \n13:30 –Leaving from Baku to Gobustan (1 way takes 45 min)\n \n14:30 – Arrive at Gobustan National Park\n - Visit Gobustan National Park, a UNESCO World Heritage site known for its ancient petroglyphs, rock formations, and archaeological heritage dating back more than 40,000 years. The open-air museum offers insights into prehistoric human life, hunting traditions, and early settlements. After exploring the site, continue to the nearby Mud Volcanoes—one of the largest mud volcano fields in the world. The unique grey, lunar-like landscape and constantly bubbling mud pools create an unforgettable natural experience and an excellent spot for photos.\n \n17:00 - Leaving Gobustan to Baku \n \n18:00 – Dinner Break (if includes)\n \n19:00 – Drop to the Hotel \n \nOvernight in Baku', 36.00, 41.00, 47.00, 59.00, 189.00, 147.00, 177.00, 206.00, 206.00, 20.00, 47.00),
