(57, 'Hotel', 'Absheron + Old City Tour', 'Private Transfer', NULL, NULL, NULL, '10:00 – Leaving Baku to Absheron (1 way x 30 mins)\n\n10:30 – Visit to Fire Temple (Ateshgah)\n - An ancient Zoroastrian site where flames were historically kept burning as part of religious rituals. The temple provides insight into Azerbaijan’s early religious history and Zoroastrian culture. Visitors can explore the site and learn about the traditions of fire worship.\n \n11.30 - Burning Mountains (Yanardag)\n A natural gas hillside that has been burning continuously for decades, creating a unique “burning mountain” phenomenon. It is a famous landmark of Azerbaijan, offering visitors spectacular views and a memorable experience of the country’s natural fiery landscape.\n \n12:30 – Leaving Absheron to Baku\n \n13:00 – Lunch Break\n \n14:30 - Old City tour starts from Shamakhi Gates followed by below places (Photo stop):\n - Shamakhi Gates – The historic entrance to the Old City, showcasing iconic stone architecture.\n - Sculptures of Azim Azimzadeh – Artistic monuments honoring Azerbaijan’s famed satirical painter and graphic artist.\n - Caravanserai of Bukhara – A restored medieval inn once used by Silk Road traders for rest and trade.\n - Caravanserai of Multani – A traditional guesthouse built for merchants from Multan, reflecting oriental caravan culture.\n - Maiden’s Tower – Baku’s mysterious UNESCO-listed tower offering panoramic views of the Old City.\n - Bazar Square – A lively historic square once serving as the commercial heart of Icherisheher.\n - Miniature Books’ Museum – A unique museum displaying one of the world’s largest collections of tiny books.\n - Shirvanshahs’ Palace – A majestic 15th-century royal complex showcasing medieval Azerbaijani architecture.\n \n18:00 – Dinner Break (if includes)\n \n19:00 – Drop to the Hotel \n \nOvernight in Baku', 41.00, 47.00, 47.00, 59.00, 118.00, 147.00, 177.00, 206.00, 206.00, 20.00, 47.00),
